;; day8/re-frame2-hicasso — the Hicasso view substrate.
;;
;; Hicasso is a lean-React substrate: a boundary is a real React function
;; component minted by `defview`, and the runtime owns exactly the three
;; things React does not — which boundaries a commit must re-run, how a
;; body reaches subscription values, and the fence that keeps one render
;; pass on one commit. The public door is `re-frame.hicasso`; everything
;; else is `re-frame.hicasso.impl.*` and is not a consumer surface.
;;
;; rf2-hic-001 established this artefact by copying the measured
;; prototype out of the benchmark tree
;; (implementation/freehand/test/re_frame/bench/hicasso/{front,arm1}/)
;; with namespaces renamed and nothing else changed. `frozen-sources.edn`
;; beside `src/` pins each donor file by digest so that claim stays true;
;; `scripts/check_freeze.py` is what checks it.
;;
;; DEPENDENCIES. Core alone. Every substrate namespace the runtime reaches
;; for — `re-frame.adapter.context`, `re-frame.live-frame`,
;; `re-frame.late-bind`, `re-frame.registrar`, `re-frame.performance`,
;; `re-frame.trace`, `re-frame.interop` — is core's, and routing is reached
;; through core's late-bind registry rather than by dependency, so the
;; packaging graph stays `hicasso -> core late-bind <- routing` with no
;; cycle (Conventions §Packaging). React itself is an npm dependency,
;; declared in implementation/package.json, not here.
;;
;; NO :clein / :clein/build, deliberately. This artefact is pre-publication:
;; it carries no Maven coordinate and is absent from the lockstep array and
;; the release deploy matrix, exactly as `ui` and `freehand` are. Release
;; wiring is rf2-hic-008's, not this bead's, and the lockstep gate
;; inventories publishable artefacts by the presence of `:aliases/:clein/build`
;; — so adding one here would enlist an artefact that has nothing to ship.
;;
;; `resources` is on :paths for ONE reason: the clj-kondo export
;; (rf2-hic-022) reaches a consumer over the CLASSPATH. `clj-kondo --lint
;; "$(clojure -Spath)" --dependencies --copy-configs` scans the classpath for
;; `clj-kondo.exports/<group>/<artifact>/`, so an export directory that is not
;; on :paths is simply invisible — and the failure mode is silence rather than
;; an error. `lint_export_test.clj` asserts this line rather than trusting it.
;; Nothing under `resources/` is a loadable namespace: the hook file is data
;; that clj-kondo's own SCI reads from the config directory.
{:paths ["src" "resources"]
 :deps  {day8/re-frame2 {:local/root "../core"}}

 :aliases
 ;; This alias was classpath-probe-only until rf2-hic-022, on the grounds
 ;; that the runtime requires React, so every suite the artefact owns is
 ;; CLJS and runs on the Node lane (`re-frame.hicasso.*-cljs-test`, compiled
 ;; by the `:node-test-hicasso` shadow-cljs build). `--probe` waived the
 ;; runner's test-count floor as a declared exemption, and said in terms:
 ;; "if a JVM-runnable suite ever lands in `test/`, drop `--probe` and take
 ;; the floor."
 ;;
 ;; One has. `re-frame.hicasso.lint-export-test` runs clj-kondo in process
 ;; over the artefact's own lint export — no React, no DOM, no CLJS compile,
 ;; and nothing about it belongs on the Node lane. So the floor is taken.
 ;;
 ;; NO AUTOMATED LANE RUNS THIS YET, and that is recorded rather than
 ;; papered over: there is no `jvm-hicasso` job in `.github/workflows/
 ;; test.yml`, and the roster↔CI bijection gate (rf2-as6bg) correctly refuses
 ;; a `scripts/test-jvm-implementation.sh` entry without one. `test.yml` is
 ;; hot-zone, so that pairing is a scheduling decision. Until it lands, run
 ;; this suite by hand: `cd implementation/hicasso && clojure -M:test`.
 ;;
 ;; clj-kondo is TEST-ONLY and pinned to the version CI's own lint job
 ;; installs (`.github/workflows/lint.yml`), because two clj-kondo versions
 ;; disagree about which findings are errors, and a suite that asserts on
 ;; findings must be asserting about the build the project actually gates on.
 {:test {:extra-paths ["test"
                       ;; rf2-hic-020 — `re-frame.hicasso.test`, the supported
                       ;; L0–L2 testing surface. Its own root, and NOT in
                       ;; `:paths` above: a consumer that never writes a test
                       ;; never carries it, so the kit's zero production
                       ;; reachability is a packaging fact rather than a
                       ;; convention. Listed here so the classpath probe sees
                       ;; it; the CLJS lane reaches it through the
                       ;; `hicasso/test_kit/src` :source-paths entry in
                       ;; implementation/shadow-cljs.edn.
                       "test_kit/src"]
         :extra-deps  {clj-kondo/clj-kondo       {:mvn/version "2026.04.15"}
                       day8/re-frame2-test-quiet {:local/root "../test-quiet"}
                       ;; The Node lane's substrate. The prototype's own
                       ;; node-lane suites run on the UIx adapter and not on
                       ;; plain-atom, because plain-atom has no reactivity
                       ;; layer — a subscription under it never notifies, so
                       ;; every commit assertion would pass vacuously by
                       ;; never firing. Test-only: shipping source names no
                       ;; adapter at all.
                       day8/re-frame2-uix {:local/root "../adapters/uix"}}
         :main-opts   ["-m" "re-frame.test-quiet.runner"]}}}
